    description: "Currently AGENTS.md \"Axis declaration for multi-value fields\" rule and ADR-0024 §\"Creation practice\" rely on **author discipline** to notice when a PR adds a multi-value field to a core dataclass and therefore needs an axis-declaration ADR. ADR-0024 §3 open question 2 explicitly flags this as automatable but defers it: \"Pre-commit detection of new multi-value field additions — the creation practice currently relies on documentation. Worth automating? Detection requires AST inspection of `@dataclass` definitions for fields whose type narrows (Literal vs. str), or a manual hint annotation. Tracker as a follow-on if drift surfaces.\"\n\nThis item is the follow-on. It is **not** urgent; it should land only if drift surfaces — i.e., a multi-value field gets added to `ir.py` / `datamodels.py` without an accompanying axis-declaration ADR or a documented \"no axis needed\" rationale. If that happens once, file a BACKFILL sub-item to fix the missed declaration; if it happens twice, this item is the structural fix. P4.\n\n# Scope\n\nPre-commit detection that fires when a PR introduces or modifies a multi-value field on a core dataclass without either (a) reusing an existing axis registry, (b) introducing a new axis registry alongside, or (c) declaring \"single-value or small bounded enum — no axis needed\" in the dataclass docstring.\n\n# Detection signals (in order of robustness)\n\n1. **AST inspection of `@dataclass` definitions** in `packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/ir.py`, `datamodels.py`, and any other file annotated as a \"core dataclass file\" via a sentinel comment.\n   - For each new or modified field whose type annotation is `str` (or `Optional[str]`, `str | None`, etc.), flag as a candidate multi-value field.\n   - For each field whose type is a `Literal[...]` with >5 values, flag as definitely multi-value.\n   - For each field whose type is an `Enum` subclass with >5 members, flag as definitely multi-value.\n\n2. **Manual hint annotation** as an escape hatch:\n   - `# axis: <axis-name>` comment on the field's line indicates the field is on the named axis (must exist in some registry).\n   - `# axis: bounded-enum` comment indicates the author has decided no axis is needed (small enum, documented in docstring).\n   - `# axis: pending` comment indicates the author acknowledges the field is multi-value but defers the axis decision (with a tracker item ID required: `# axis: pending WI-xxxxx`).\n\n3. **Registry cross-reference**: if the field's annotation cites an axis (via `Literal[*MY_AXIS_VALUES]` or similar), the linter resolves the axis and confirms the values are in the registry. Otherwise the field must have a `# axis:` comment.\n\n# Implementation shape\n\n- New script `scripts/check-multi-value-field-axis-declaration` analogous to `scripts/check-edge-type-drift`.\n- Wires into `.githooks/pre-commit` skipping when no `packages/*/src/**/ir.py` or `**/datamodels.py` files (or any file with the sentinel comment) are staged.\n- Property test mirroring `test_edge_types.py::test_no_drift` — runs the linter against the live tree.\n- Errors are advisory by default (warning), can be made blocking via `STRICT=1` env var, mirroring how `scripts/check-edge-type-drift` evolves.\n\n# Acceptance criteria\n\nA1. Linter exists at `scripts/check-multi-value-field-axis-declaration` and runs in <2 seconds on the full tree.\nA2. Wired into `.githooks/pre-commit` with the staged-file filter.\nA3. Property test in `packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/` calling the linter's underlying function.\nA4. Documented in AGENTS.md replacing the prose-only \"Axis declaration for multi-value fields\" rule with a reference to the linter.\nA5. ADR-0024 §3 open question 2 marked \"Resolved by WI-<this-item-ID>\" in a Status section update.\nA6. Existing fields on `Edge`, `Symbol`, `Span` that pre-date the linter all pass (i.e., have either a registry-backed annotation or a `# axis: bounded-enum` comment with docstring justification, retroactively added).\n\n# When to land\n\nP4 because this is preventive automation, not a fix for an active failure. Land when:\n- A multi-value-field-without-axis incident occurs in production code (justifying the structural fix), OR\n- The cadence-hook periodic pass would otherwise need to surface this category of drift manually for the second time, OR\n- ADR-0027 / ADR-0028 / a future axis ADR ships with new multi-value fields and the author wants the linter as scaffolding before further axis declarations.\n\n# Related\n\n- ADR-0024 §3 open question 2 (the originating defer).\n- AGENTS.md \"Axis declaration for multi-value fields\" essentialization.\n- `scripts/check-edge-type-drift` and `find_axis_drift` helper as the architectural precedent.\n- WI-rodub-bupun-... (the audit-findings reclassification item) — both items operationalize ADR-0024's discipline; this one for creation, that one for filing the verdict outputs."  # 64a2
